.TH "watch" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
watch \- Subscribe the change stream of the collection space
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]SdbCS.watch( [token], [options] )\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
SdbCS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to subscribe the change stream of the collection space.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \[bu] 2
token (\f[I]StreamToken, optional\f[])
.RS 2
.PP
Specifies the starting position of this change stream.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
options (\f[I]object, optional\f[])
.RS 2
.IP \[bu] 2
ChangeTypes (\f[I]string\f[])
.RS 2
.PP
The type of change events to subscribe to.
Supported types include "RECORD" (BSON record DML operations), "LOB" (LOB DML
operations), "DDL" (DDL operations), "TRANS" (transaction change operations),
"ALL" (all types).
Multiple types can be connected with "|", and it is not case sensitive.
The default is: "RECORD|DDL".
.PP
Format: \f[C]ChangeTypes: "RECORD|DDL"\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
MaxWaitTime (\f[I]integer\f[])
.RS 2
.PP
Specifies the maximum waiting time when there is no new data, in seconds.
After the timeout, the change stream will return an empty control type record.
Less than 0 means waiting indefinitely, 0 means no waiting.
Default: 1 second.
.PP
Format: \f[C]MaxWaitTime: 1\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
CacheSize (\f[I]integer\f[])
.RS 2
.PP
The amount of log data to cache, in MB.
The range is 0~2048, where 0 means no cache setting, and the maximum is 2 GB.
Default: 32.
Logs that exceed the cache size will need to be read from the log file.
.PP
Format: \f[C]CacheSize: 32\f[]
.RE
.RE
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
If the function executes successfully, it will return an SdbCursor type object.
The returned change stream data can be obtained through this object.
.PP
If the function execution fails, it will throw an exception and output error
information.
